@startuml SequenceDiagram
title Bankitis Online Banking System - UML Sequence Diagram (Money Transfer Flow)

autonumber
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

actor Customer as "Bank Customer" #LightSkyBlue
participant Client as "Client UI (React/Vite)" #LightYellow
participant Action as "Banking Engine" #LightGreen
participant DB as "Banking State & Ledger" #LightCyan
participant Notif as "Notification Dispatcher" #MistyRose

Customer -> Client : 1. Enters recipient UPI ID (e.g. devika@bank)
Client -> Action : 2. resolveRecipientAction("devika@bank")
Action -> DB : 3. Lookup account by upiId = 'devika@bank'
DB --> Action : 4. Returns Account and User details
Action --> Client : 5. Return { success: true, recipientName: "Devika" }
Client --> Customer : 6. Displays verified recipient badge

Customer -> Client : 7. Enters Amount, Category & Note
Customer -> Client : 8. Enters 6-Digit UPI PIN & clicks "Confirm & Pay"
Client -> Action : 9. transferMoney(recipient, amount, pin, note)

group Atomic Transaction Execution
  Action -> Action : 10. Verify 6-digit PIN & check rate limiting
  Action -> DB : 11. Lock and verify sender balance >= transfer amount
  Action -> DB : 12. Deduct sender balance
  Action -> DB : 13. Credit receiver balance
  Action -> DB : 14. Record Transaction ledger entry (Ref: TXN-YYYYMMDD-XXXXXX)
  Action -> DB : 15. Write security AuditLog entry
  Action -> DB : 16. Commit transaction atomically
end

Action -> Notif : 17. Dispatch in-app debit/credit alerts
Notif --> Action : 18. Alerts queued / logged
Action --> Client : 19. Return { success: true, referenceNumber, updatedBalance }
Client --> Customer : 20. Render Success Receipt modal & update available balance

@enduml

